<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87647" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προκατα-γιγνώσκω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>vote against beforehand, condemn
				by a prejudgement,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				21.227
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				21.42.2
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ προκαταγίγνωσκ᾽ . . , πρὶν ἄν γ᾽
					ἀκούσῃς ἀμφοτέρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>V.</u>
					919
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μὴ προκατεγνωκέναι μηδέν</span>
			not to <i>prejudge</i> in any point, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.2
			</span></i>: generally, <i>condemn, disapprove of in advance,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				12.260
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> c.
			inf., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἡμῶν . . ἥσσους
				εἶναι</span>
			<i>prejudge</i> us and say we are . . , <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				3.53
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφῶν αὐτῶν π. ἀδικεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					20.21
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀδικεῖν</span> (without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινος</span>) <i><span class="en">
				And.
				1.3
			</span></i>; also 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ὡς ἀδικῶ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aeschin.
					2.7
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τινὸς φόνον</span>
			<i>give a verdict of</i> murder <i>against</i> one
				<i>beforehand,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				5.85
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τινῶν ἄδικόν τι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀδικίαν τινός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					19.10
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. θανατόν τινος</span>
			<i>pass sentence</i> of death <i>on before,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				18.60
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὴν τιμωρίαν αὐτὸς σαυτοῦ π.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.C.
					46.11
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
